1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,505
Agents do not fail only because they forget.

2
00:00:03,505 --> 00:00:09,200
They fail when yesterday's truth is remembered as if it were still true.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,000
One source says Redis.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,800
A proposal says Postgres.

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,050
The pull request implements Postgres.

6
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:16,850
Retrieval returns every sentence.

7
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:25,400
Lacuna keeps the sources, marks what changed, exposes conflict, and refuses to turn missing evidence into a confident answer.

8
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:29,434
We built Lacuna, a provenance-first memory layer on HydraDB.

9
00:00:29,434 --> 00:00:32,572
Conversations become evidence, claims, entities, and relationships.

10
00:00:32,572 --> 00:00:38,400
Lacuna resolves what stands now, then compiles the context the next agent needs.

11
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,661
Here is the deployed product.

12
00:00:40,661 --> 00:00:44,730
I ask, Who is the runbook owner for billing-gate?

13
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:51,965
Lacuna says the sources disagree, keeps both claims at equal weight, and attaches a contradiction trace.

14
00:00:51,965 --> 00:00:54,226
Ask for Foxglove's connection-pool size.

15
00:00:54,226 --> 00:00:59,200
Nothing states one, so Lacuna returns never stated, instead of guessing.

16
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,006
The answer stays inspectable.

17
00:01:01,006 --> 00:01:03,714
A table keeps every memory readable.

18
00:01:03,714 --> 00:01:11,389
On the accepted public build, the overview measured four hundred fifty-three nodes and six hundred eighty-two edges.

19
00:01:11,389 --> 00:01:15,000
The proof view follows one exact source-to-evidence-to-claim-to-entity path.

20
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,816
Memory becomes bounded work.

21
00:01:16,816 --> 00:01:20,903
Lacuna includes two built-in, no-write roles: Researcher and Reviewer.

22
00:01:20,903 --> 00:01:27,259
A production run persisted eight events, tool calls, handoff, artifacts, and its final verdict.

23
00:01:27,259 --> 00:01:29,076
A daily schedule persists.

24
00:01:29,076 --> 00:01:31,800
Cross-instance exactly-once dispatch is not claimed.

25
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:37,133
One resolved context reaches web, C L I, and M C P.

26
00:01:37,133 --> 00:01:46,911
The parity sweep sends all sixty-four questions through the C L I and both M C P transports, then compares every field.

27
00:01:46,911 --> 00:01:47,800
They match.

28
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:52,244
The H T T P A P I is live.

29
00:01:52,244 --> 00:01:55,800
A packaged S D K is not shipped.

30
00:01:55,800 --> 00:02:01,578
The voice surface models fifteen explicit states, including listening, interruption, and typed fallback.

31
00:02:01,578 --> 00:02:05,578
This narration uses the verified Vaibhav Lalwani professional clone.

32
00:02:05,578 --> 00:02:11,800
The product's live voice round-trip remains separately gated until its server key is configured.

33
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:15,752
HydraDB is the retrieval substrate, not a results bucket.

34
00:02:15,752 --> 00:02:18,387
A correction becomes a supersession edge.

35
00:02:18,387 --> 00:02:24,096
Provenance is the path from session to message to evidence span to claim.

36
00:02:24,096 --> 00:02:25,413
Disagreement is structural.

37
00:02:25,413 --> 00:02:28,048
Multi-hop answers traverse a bridge entity.

38
00:02:28,048 --> 00:02:32,000
No claim means absence, not a low similarity score.

39
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:39,703
On the labelled generated evaluation, Lacuna answers sixty-four of sixty-four with zero unsupported answers using about eighteen context tokens.

40
00:02:39,703 --> 00:02:43,757
The strongest tuned baseline reaches sixty-three using about eighteen hundred.

41
00:02:43,757 --> 00:02:47,000
Self-hosted and HydraDB Cloud matched field by field.

42
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,642
Models can change.

43
00:02:48,642 --> 00:02:50,283
Agents can change.

44
00:02:50,283 --> 00:02:54,114
The memory stays current, inspectable, and portable.

45
00:02:54,114 --> 00:02:57,398
Lacuna: memory that knows what changed.
